{
  "an3.65:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.65 ",
  "an3.65:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "an3.65:0.3": "With the Kālāmas of Kesamutta ",
  "an3.65:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "an3.65:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was wandering in the land of the Kosalans together with a large Saṅgha of mendicants when he arrived at a town of the Kālāmas named Kesamutta. ",
  "an3.65:1.3": "The Kālāmas of Kesamutta heard: ",
  "an3.65:1.4": "“It seems the ascetic Gotama—a Sakyan, gone forth from a Sakyan family—has arrived at Kesamutta. ",
  "an3.65:1.5": "He has this good reputation: ",
  "an3.65:1.6": "‘That Blessed One is perfected, a fully awakened Buddha …’ ",
  "an3.65:1.7": "It’s good to see such perfected ones.” ",
  "an3.65:2.1": "Then the Kālāmas went up to the Buddha. Before sitting down to one side, some bowed, some exchanged greetings and polite conversation, some held up their cupped palms toward the Buddha, some announced their name and clan, while some kept silent. Seated to one side the Kālāmas said to the Buddha: ",
  "an3.65:3.1": "“There are, sir, some ascetics and brahmins who come to Kesamutta. ",
  "an3.65:3.2": "They explain and promote only their own doctrine, while they attack, badmouth, disparage, and smear the doctrines of others. ",
  "an3.65:3.3": "Then some other ascetics and brahmins come to Kesamutta. ",
  "an3.65:3.4": "They too explain and promote only their own doctrine, while they attack, badmouth, disparage, and smear the doctrines of others. ",
  "an3.65:3.5"